{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.1146/annurev.pa.36.040196.002333\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"8725398","source":"MED","pmid":"8725398","doi":"10.1146/annurev.pa.36.040196.002333","title":"Complexity and diversity of mammalian adenylyl cyclases.","authorString":"Sunahara RK, Dessauer CW, Gilman AG.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Sunahara RK","lastName":"Sunahara","firstName":"R K","initials":"RK","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1702-8619"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Pharmacology, University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas 75235, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Dessauer CW","lastName":"Dessauer","firstName":"C W","initials":"CW"},{"fullName":"Gilman AG","lastName":"Gilman","firstName":"A G","initials":"AG"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1702-8619"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"36","journalIssueId":945325,"dateOfPublication":"1996 ","monthOfPublication":0,"yearOfPublication":1996,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Annu Rev Pharmacol Toxicol","title":"Annual review of pharmacology and toxicology","essn":"1545-4304","issn":"0362-1642","nlmid":"7607088","isoabbreviation":"Annu Rev Pharmacol Toxicol"},"printPublicationDate":"1996-01-01"},"pubYear":"1996","pageInfo":"461-480","abstractText":"Molecular cloning has permitted identification of several novel isoforms of mammalian adenylyl cyclase; these proteins now comprise a family of at least 10. All of the membrane-bound enzymes are activated by the alpha subunit of G alpha, a receptor-regulated, heterotrimeric guanine nucleotide-binding protein, and by the diterpene forskolin. Certain cyclases are also activated by Ca(2+)-calmodulin, while some are inhibited by the alpha subunits of the three Gi proteins. The discovery of new isoforms has also revealed unanticipated mechanisms of regulation, including activation or inhibition by the G-protein beta gamma subunit complex, inhibition by G(o) alpha, inhibition by Ca2+, and phosphorylation by protein kinases C and A. The effects of activators are often highly synergistic or conditional, suggesting function of these enyzmes as coincidence detectors. The plethora of receptors, G proteins, and adenylyl cyclases permits assembly of very complex signaling systems with a wide variety of integrative characteristics.","affiliation":"Department of Pharmacology, University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas 75235, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Review","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Calcium","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"GTP-Binding Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Isoenzymes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IP","qualifierName":"isolation & purification"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cyclic AMP-Dependent Protein Kinases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Protein Kinase C","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","q